## 2. Voice recording — all rights reserved

Applies to `assets/sfx/voice.m4a` and the alternate takes in `assets/sfx/takes/`.

Performed and recorded by Helen Allien Poe. Not covered by the MIT licence above,
and not granted for reuse. It is a person singing to her brother; treat it the way
you would the portrait in section 3.

The lyric is sung to the cadence of Haddaway's "What Is Love" (1993, written by
Dee Dee Halligan and Junior Torello). The words are original and so is the
recording; the melody is not, and remains the property of its writers and their
publishers.

## 3. Photography, logos and branding — all rights reserved

Applies to everything under `assets/pieces/`, `assets/bg/`, `assets/logo/` and
`assets/portrait/`, and to the source photography in `choosed/` and
`PROMO_Auris/` (which is not committed to this repository).

**None of it is covered by the MIT licence above.** It is included so this
specific game can be built and played, and is not granted for reuse,
redistribution or modification.

- **Auris** jewellery photography, the "AURIS" name and the Auris monogram.
- **Saint Scalpelburg** studio photography and the Scalpelburg logo
  (`assets/logo/scalpelburg.png`), which is a separate business and a separate
  mark from Auris.
- **`assets/portrait/vlad.jpg`** — a portrait of Vlad Bodmodov, used with his
  family's knowledge. "Vlad Bodmodov" is a working name and he is a public figure
  in his trade, with a comparable portrait already published on his studio's own
  site, so this is his professional persona rather than private information. It
  still is not a design asset: it belongs to this gift, and a forked or
  promotional version needs his actual agreement, not merely the absence of an
  objection.

Anyone forking this repository for the code must replace all of it with their
own material.


## 4. A note on the celebrate cue

`celebrate` has no committed audio file. The cue synthesises an original sting in
`src/sfx.js` and is covered by the MIT licence in section 1.

If a `celebrate` audio file is added locally, it is covered by whatever terms
that recording carries, and this file should be updated to say so. A commercial
recording is not licensed for public or promotional use merely by being placed in
this folder.

### Making a build that is clear of the melody

The only borrowed thing in this repository is the tune the voice track is sung to
(section 2). Removing it is deleting one file:

    rm assets/sfx/voice.m4a assets/sfx/takes/*.m4a

`celebrate` then falls back to the synthesised sting, which is original and needs
no clearance. Nothing else changes and no code is touched. That is the build to
use for anything published under the Auris or Scalpelburg name.
